/* config — a tiny configuration file parser.

   Reads a simple key=value format where values can be text (quoted),
   numbers, or booleans (true/false). Stores them in an atlas (a map
   whose values are a union type) and uses Judge to dispatch on the
   value type when printing.

   Exercises:
   - atlas (heterogeneous map)
   - Judge over a closed union (no Otherwise needed)
   - In-branch narrowing via If and Judge
   - Fallible parsing with Try to auto-unwrapping
*/

Bind (text or number or fact) or failure to parse-value, given (the text raw):
    Define clean as raw trimmed.
    If clean is "true", return true.
    If clean is "false", return false.
    
    Define num as clean converted to number.
    If num is not void, return num.
    
    Define len as the length of clean.
    If len is 2 or more:
        Define first as the characters from 1 to 1 of clean.
        Define last as the characters from len to len of clean.
        If first is "\"" and last is "\"", return the characters from 2 to len - 1 of clean.
    Done.
    
    Return a failure "unrecognized value format".
Done.

Bind atlas from text to (text or number or fact) to parse-config, given (the text source):
    Define config as an atlas from text to (text or number or fact).
    Define lines as source split by "\n".
    For each line in lines, repeat:
        Define clean as line trimmed.
        If the length of clean is 0, skip.
        
        Define eq-pos as the position of "=" in clean.
        If eq-pos is not void:
            Define setting as (the characters from 1 to eq-pos - 1 of clean) trimmed.
            Define val-raw as the characters from eq-pos + 1 to the end of clean.
            
            Try to:
                Define val as cast parse-value on (val-raw).
                In config, the entry for setting becomes val.
            Done.
            In case of failure:
                State "warning: skipping invalid line: {clean}".
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.
    Return config.
Done.

Bind void to print-config, given (the atlas from text to (text or number or fact) config):
    State "loaded configuration:".
    For each pair in config, repeat:
        Define setting as the key of pair.
        Define val as the value of pair.
        Judge val, where it is:
            A text, state "  {setting} = \"{it}\" (text)".
            A number, state "  {setting} = {it converted to text} (number)".
            A fact, state "  {setting} = {it converted to text} (fact)".
        Done.
    Done.
Done.

Bind void to use-config, given (the atlas from text to (text or number or fact) config):
    State "".
    State "using configuration:".
    
    Define host as the entry for "host" in config.
    If host is not void:
        If host is a text, state "  connecting to {host}...".
    Done.
    
    Define port as the entry for "port" in config.
    If port is not void:
        If port is a number, state "  on port {port converted to text}.".
    Done.
    
    Define debug as the entry for "debug" in config.
    If debug is not void:
        If debug is a fact:
            If debug is true, state "  debug mode is ON.".
            Otherwise, state "  debug mode is OFF.".
        Done.
    Done.
Done.

Bind void to play:
    Define source as "examples/config.txt".
    Try to:
        Define content as read all from the file source.
        Define normalized as replace "\r" with "" in content.   // CRLF insurance on Windows
        Define config as cast parse-config on (normalized).
        Cast print-config on (config).
        Cast use-config on (config).
    Done.
    In case of failure:
        Define msg as the message of the failure.
        State "could not read {source}: {msg}".
    Done.
Done.

Cast play.